170 - Come, You Faithful
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 170
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[F]Come, you [C/E]faithful, [Dm]raise [C]the [F]strain
[Bb]Of triumphant [C]gladness;
[Bb/D]God [F]has [C]brought [F]His Israel
[C/E]Into [Dm]joy [C]from [F]sadness;
[F]Loosed from [Gm]Pharoah's [Am]bitter [F]yoke
[F]Jacob's sons [Bb]and daughters;
[C]Led them [Bb/D]with [F]unmoistened foot
[C]Through the [Dm]Red [Am]Sea [Dm/F]waters.

Verse 2:
[F]'Tis the [C/E]spring of [Dm]souls [C]today;
[Bb]Christ has burst [C]His prison,
[Bb/D]And from [F]three [C]days'sleep [F]in death
[C/E]As a [Dm]sun [C]has [F]risen;
[F]All the [Gm]winter [Am]of [Gm/Bb]our [F]sins,
[F]Long and dark, [Bb]is flying
